# Two Jace's Machinations, the second cast in response to the first. The second resolves first and makes the Jace token
# with 8 loyalty; the first puts 8 more on that same token rather than making another (the ruling: "If you control a
# Jace planeswalker token, you can't choose to create a new one"), so one token has 16.
#
# Two permissions to activate loyalty abilities at instant speed are still one loyalty activation per permanent each
# turn (CR 606.3): in Bot1's own end step - its own turn, but no main phase - the token's -1 is activated, and after it
# resolves no other ability of the token is offered.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Jace's Machinations
Jace's Machinations
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Jace's Machinations.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Jace's Machinations.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 8
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 16
[T1 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Activate(Ability: Surveil)
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Activate

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 15
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
